.TH MOUNT 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
mount \- mount a filesystem, or list mounted filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount
\fISOURCE\fR \fITARGET\fR \fB\-t\fR \fIFSTYPE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments, list currently mounted filesystems (reads Linux's /proc/mounts). With SOURCE, TARGET, and \fB\-t\fR FSTYPE, attempt a real mount(2) call.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
mitosOS has no mount table exposed to userspace yet.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the mount table or mount(2) call failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
